content.thinking:
Main code compiles. Step 7: write the new test file `BatchRecallReleaseTest.java`. Cover:

1. Happy path: 两级树 root recalled → retests PASS for all closure → apply → approve → root restored RELEASED, recall RELEASED, snapshot written, descendants unblocked.
2. Apply failures: not recalled → 409; wrong version → 409; unknown batch → 404; validation 400 (empty retestBatches, blank measures, missing approver).
3. Approval 422 branches: missing retest gap; FAILED latest retest; QUARANTINED descendant; declared set missing closure member; declared set with unknown extra; wrong approver → 422. After failure: batch still RECALLED, recall ACTIVE, no snapshot, releaseKey not consumed (retry after fix succeeds with same releaseKey... wait — the apply succeeded so releaseKey is consumed by apply; failure at approve doesn't consume approve commandKey. Test: approve fails 422 → fix retests → approve again with same commandKey succeeds (failure didn't occupy key).
4. Idempotency: apply same releaseKey same params → same response replay; same releaseKey different params → 409. Approve same commandKey replay → same result, no duplicate snapshot.
5. 代次： release v1 → re-recall (v2) → apply with version 1 → 409; apply version 2 → approve → restored. Only covered generation released; v1 recall record remains RELEASED, v2 becomes RELEASED; both records retained.
6. Descendant historical recall not deleted: descendant itself RELEASED then recalled (own recall ACTIVE), then root recalled, root released → descendant still RECALLED, needs own retest + release.
7. Concurrency: concurrent approve vs concurrent FAIL retest — commit order decides; concurrent same-commandKey approve → both 201 same body; concurrent apply same releaseKey same params → both 201.
8. Queries: recall-impact, retest-gaps, release detail.

Also note: existing tests clean tables in @BeforeEach — new test must also delete from new tables (retest, recall_release, recall_release_snapshot). Existing test classes don't know about new tables — but they delete all batches etc. Since new tables reference batch_key without FK, leftover rows in retest/recall_release from my tests could affect other test classes? Other test classes use unique keys per test (UUID), so leftover rows won't collide. But my own test class must clean new tables. Also releaseKey uniqueness: I use unique keys.

Wait — one issue: existing tests' cleanTables don't delete retest/recall_release/recall_release_snapshot. If my tests run before others, leftovers remain but keyed by unique keys — no interference. Fine.

Test helper design — model on BatchSplitLineageTest. Let me write the test file now.

Key flows to set up:
- createBatch(key, items, expected)
- releaseBatch(key, inspector) — needs history GET to find requiredTests
- split(...)
- recall(key, actor, reason, ck, expected)
- retest(key, retestKey, outcome, inspector, ck, expected)
- applyRelease(key, actor, releaseKey, version, measures, retestBatches, approver, expected)
- approveRelease(key, releaseKey, actor, ck, expected)
- currentStatus, availableKeys

Happy path scenario:
```
root = create + release
split root -> [child, sibling]
releaseBatch(child) → RELEASED
submitTest(sibling...) leave sibling QUARANTINED? No wait — quarantined descendant blocks approval ("无未决隔离"). For happy path, all descendants must be non-QUARANTINED and have PASS retest. Let's make: child RELEASED, sibling PENDING_RELEASE (submit its test PASS).
recall(root) → root RECALLED, descendants blocked.
retest PASS for root, child, sibling.
apply: releaseKey RK-1, version 1, measures, retestBatches [root, child, sibling] (unsorted, with duplicate to test normalization), approver "qa-lead".
→ 201, response retestBatches sorted.
approve by "qa-lead" → 201 snapshot with closureBatches sorted [child, root, sibling]... sorted lexicographically.
assert root status RELEASED (prior status), available contains root/child/sibling again.
recall record: recall_status RELEASED, released_at not null.
snapshot query: GET detail → release.status APPROVED, snapshot non-null, closureBatches matches.
descendant historical: child has no recall record.
```

Failure branches test:
```
root released, split → child (QUARANTINED, no tests), sibling released.
recall root.
retest PASS root, sibling; child none.
apply RK-2 with retestBatches [root, child, sibling] → 201.
approve → 422 (child QUARANTINED → PENDING_QUARANTINE... wait order: unknown check, missing check, quarantine check, retest check. child is QUARANTINED → 422 "未决隔离". Also child missing retest. Quarantine checked first.)
